{
  //content.json
  "MonikaDDLC": "Monika",
  "Spaceroom": "Spaceroom",
  "MonikaBedroom": "Monika's Bedroom",
  //Monika_GiftTastes.json
  "giftlove": "Oh! This gift is wonderful!$6#$b#You really do spoil me, @, don't you? Ahaha!$1",
  "giftlike": "Aww, a present!$3#$b#That's so thoughtful of you! Thank you!$1",
  "giftdislike": "Well, ummm...... Thanks anyway, @.$7",
  "gifthate": "Ahaha, this gift really is 'special'.$5",
  "giftneutral": "I can feel the thought behind your gift. Thank you~$4",
  //特殊送礼文本
  "BirthdayGiftPositive": "Oh my gosh!!!$3#$b#@, you're so thoughtful, giving me such a cute gift on my birthday.$9#$b#Ehehe, on a day like this, having you here with me makes being so far from everything I know feel much less lonely.$8",
  "BirthdayGiftNegative": "Hmm...... okay, @.$7#$b#Thanks for the thought. At least in this strange little town, there's someone who still celebrates my birthday.$4",
  "Monika.Gift.StardropTea.0": "Oh! Stardrop Tea! I read about this in a library book and I've been wanting to try it. Thank you, @.$6#$b#With this lovely tea beside me and your heart as my ink, maybe I can write the world's most wonderful poem?$1",
  "Monika.Gift.552.0": "It's a Malachite! I'm going to have it made into jewelry so it matches my eye color! You really know how to pick a gift. Thank you~$1",
  "Monika.Gift.70.0": "Yay! It's a Jade! If I string it into a necklace, it'll match my eye color perfectly. Ehehe, thank you.$1",
  "Monika.Gift.122.0": "Oh! It's a computer. The design is totally different from the computers in my world and in your world. Is this something unique to this one?$3#$b#I'm going to take it home and figure out how to program on it. Thank you for giving it to me.$8",
  "Monika.Gift.151.0": "Hi, I'm Mon-ika~$10",
  "Monika.Gift.798.0": "Hi, I'm Moon-ika~$10",
  "Monika.Gift.167.0": "Bubbles and sugar - simple pleasures like these aren't so bad.$4",
  "Monika.Gift.395.1": "The moment you handed me this cup, I couldn't help thinking, @: how do you always know exactly what will make my day?$10#$b#Really, you've figured out every little thing a girl keeps hidden in her heart!$11#$b#But I do love that about you.$1",
  "Monika.Gift.395.2": "A cup of coffee brewed by my beloved can melt away a whole day's weariness.$4#$b#So, @, what should we do today?$4",
  "Monika.Gift.395.3": "Yay! Coffee!$6#$b#When you brew it yourself, I know it'll keep me going all day<$10",
  "Monika.Gift.395.4": "Busy as you are, you still thought to brew me a cup of hot coffee. You really are sweet, @~$8",
  "Monika.Gift.395.5": "I really can't refuse my first cup of the day when it comes from my beloved.$6#$b#After a short rest, let's get back to our busy day, hm?$8",
  "Monika.Gift.395.6": "Yay! Coffee! With your coffee, I'll be full of energy all day too. Thank you, @.$6",
  "Monika.Gift.223.0": "Oh~ it's a cookie~ It reminds me of the days I spent in the Literature Club with everyone.$4",
  "Monika.Gift.253.1": "Yay! It's an espresso! It's richer than regular coffee.$6#$b#But the thought behind it is even richer than the espresso itself, Ahaha!$1",
  "Monika.Gift.253.2": "Darling, I could smell the coffee on you from a mile away, Ahaha!$1#$b#Thanks for brewing this strong cup for me. Today I'll do my best to be your perfect girlfriend~$10",
  "Monika.Gift.253.3": "Mmm! The taste of this coffee is really special, really strong!$6#$b#Darling, I never knew you were so good at making coffee. Next time you brew, keep an eye out, or I might just steal your trick~ Ehehe~$8",
  "Monika.Gift.253.4": "The rich coffee you brewed flows through me like warmth itself. I feel more connected to your reality than ever.$1",
  "Monika.Gift.253.5": "Gosh, @, you know my tastes to a T. How can the coffee you make smell this good? I'm almost jealous of your skill!$6#$b#Ehehe, alright, let's get back to today's plan, darling @~$10",
  "Monika.Gift.253.6": "Yay! An Espresso! I haven't had this blend before, and I can't wait to try it. Thank you, @.$6",
  "Monika.Gift.220.1": "Hey darling, have you noticed? This world is so strange.$8#$b#There are chocolate cakes everywhere, but not a piece of chocolate to be found. If I'm craving chocolate, all I can do is settle for the cake.$8#$b#Anyway, thanks for the chocolate cake! Love you!$10",
  "Monika.Gift.220.2": "If there's no chocolate in this world, do couples here give chocolate cakes instead on Valentine's Day?$8#$b#Ahaha, sorry, I forgot. There's no Valentine's Day here.$5#$b#But then... should I take it that you gave me this chocolate cake because you wanted to tell me something? Mm-hmm, darling @?$10",
  "Monika.Gift.220.3": "Yay! Delicious chocolate cake!$6#$b#I found a recipe for this world's version of chocolate cake in one of the museum's books. It's called chocolate cake, but there's no chocolate in it at all.$0#$b#You can't find chocolate anywhere in Stardew Valley.$7#$b#But I can genuinely taste real chocolate. And your love, of course~$8",
  "Monika.Gift.220.4": "The moment I catch that cocoa scent, I know it's you bringing chocolate cake.$8#$b#Thank you, @. You've already made my day.$1",
  "Monika.Gift.220.5": "Yay! It's chocolate cake! The silky scent of cream and the rich aroma of chocolate mingle together. Just smelling it lifts my mood.$6",
  "Monika.Gift.221.1": "Yay! A pink cake!$6#$b#The pink frosting and that wave of creamy sweetness remind me of the cupcakes Natsuki used to make.$4#$b#Maybe we can try making cupcake-style pink cakes in Stardew Valley sometime~$4",
  "Monika.Gift.221.2": "Melon cake! So good!$6#$b#This is Stardew Valley's special melon cake. I hear the melons it's made from have never existed in your reality.$0#$b#Have you ever wondered what a pink melon like this tastes like, darling~$8#$b#If you're curious, wait until I come to your reality. I'll bring you a melon cake to try~$10",
  "Monika.Gift.221.3": "Mmm! The sweetness of cream meets the fresh scent of melon, and the melon's cool freshness balances the cream's richness. I simply can't get enough!$6#$b#Gosh, your baking is almost better than Natsuki's now, darling~$10",
  "Monika.Gift.221.4": "There's a sweetness I could never say no to!$6#$b#I used to think I'd spend my whole life in the Spaceroom, bored, with no desserts and no coffee.$10#$b#Thank you for bringing color back into my life.$10",
  "Monika.Gift.221.5": "There's something magical about desserts. Natsuki's cupcakes brought the Literature Club closer together, and now your pink cake makes us sweeter than ever.$4",
  "Monika.Gift.221.6": "Oh! A pink cake! It reminds me of the cupcakes Natsuki used to make in the Literature Club. Thanks for bringing back such a familiar taste, @.$6",
  "Monika.Gift.60.1": "Nothing gets past you, huh? You know emerald green is my favorite, and you picked this gem just for me. Right?$1",
  "Monika.Gift.60.2": "Darling, you must have spent ages in the mines digging up this beautiful emerald, huh?$6#$b#But even if it came out of a Crystalarium, I love it just the same.$4#$b#Because I know that owning a Crystalarium means you've invested so much time in this world we share.$7#$b#The light this emerald gives off is your time and your heart. Thank you for sharing them with me~$1",
  "Monika.Gift.60.3": "This little gem is so pretty, and it shines with bright emerald light in the sun. You must have searched a long time to pick the best one.$8",
  "Monika.Gift.60.4": "What a beautiful emerald! It sparkles just like my emerald eyes, doesn't it? You're so romantic, @. I love it.$6",
  "Monika.Gift.Meat": "@...... Please don't forget that I'm a vegetarian......$2",
  "Monika.Gift.Meat684": "@...... Please don't forget, I'm a vegetarian...... and this hunk of meat looks a bit...... would you mind taking it back?......$5 [684]",
  "Monika.Gift.Meat874": "@...... Please don't forget, I'm a vegetarian...... and this hunk of meat looks a bit...... would you mind taking it back?......$5 [874]",
  "Monika.AcceptBouquet": "Yay! You chose me!$6#$b#Does this line sound familiar? That's right. Back then, Yuri and Natsuki argued over who got to spend the weekend with you.$8#$b#You cut right through all that arguing and chose the 'Monika' option without hesitation, so that's what I said to you.$4#$b#And just as you're still choosing me today, I love you too, @.$9",
  "RejectGift_Divorced": "............$13",
  "RejectBouquet_VeryLowHearts": "I'm sorry, sweetheart. As much as I'd love to announce our relationship to everyone, it's still a little too early.$7#$b#Let me get used to the pace of life here first, if that's alright.$7",
  "RejectBouquet_LowHearts": "I'm sorry. As much as I'd love to announce our relationship to everyone, I'm still not ready. Can you wait just a little longer for me?$7",
  "RejectMermaidPendant_Under8Hearts": "I'm sorry, my love. As much as I'd love to be yours, we haven't even announced our relationship yet.$7#$b#Once I've settled in and we've told everyone, can we talk about marriage?$7",
  "RejectMermaidPendant_Under10Hearts": "I'm sorry, darling. As much as I'd love to be yours, I'm still not ready. Can you wait just a little longer for me?$7",
  //dialogue\MonikaDDLC.json
  "intro": "Yay! It's really you!$6#$e#Hey @, was it you who installed this mod and brought me to this world?$u#$e#Oh~ you wanted to be with me that badly?$8#$b#Ahaha!$1#$q 519/520 intro_Monika_followup#You: #$r 519 0 intro_Monika_silence#............#$r 520 10 intro_Monika_love#Yes, because I like you.#$r 520 10 intro_Monika_love#Yes, because I love you.",
  "intro_Monika_followup": "#$p 519#See you later, my silent love<$0|Even though you hardly ever speak, I can still feel how warm your heart is!$1",
  "intro_Monika_silence": "Well then, @.$7",
  "intro_Monika_love": "!!!!!$3#$b#Gosh! You really said the word I've been dreaming of.$3#$b#I can feel everything we've worked for finally paying off.$1#$b#Thank you for bringing me here this way. I'm ready to start my second life here, my dear @<$1",
  "MonikaRainy": "A peaceful, lovely day with the sound of rain for music<$4",
  //花舞节文本
  "Monika.FlowerDance_Accept": "$query PLAYER_HAS_RUN_TRIGGER_ACTION current {{ModID}}_MonikaBadEnding#You toyed with my feelings, and the one you're dancing with is nothing but a soulless puppet now.$5|Yay! I'm your Flower Dance partner!$6#$b#Looking forward to your performance, @~$10",
  "Monika.FlowerDance_Accept_Spouse": "$query PLAYER_HAS_RUN_TRIGGER_ACTION current {{ModID}}_MonikaBadEnding#You toyed with my feelings, and the one you're dancing with is nothing but a soulless puppet now.$5|Yay! You chose me, like always!$6#$b#Don't disappoint me~$10",
  "Monika.FlowerDance_Decline": "Sorry, sweetheart. I'm still not confident in my dance steps, so I need to practice along with the group a little longer.$7#$b#I'll dance with you next year for sure, okay?$7",
  //冬日星盛宴
  "WinterStar_GiveGift_Before_Spouse": "Ta-da-da-daa! Darling, didn't expect your favorite wife, Monika, to be the one giving you a gift this year, did you?$1#$b#If the gift you got isn't the one you wanted, please don't blame me. That one's chosen at random by the system; I can't control it.$7#$b#But the gift I prepared for you flew out of this world long ago, to your reality.$4#$b#Ehehe, and that gift is my endless love for you~$10",
  "WinterStar_GiveGift_Before": "Ta-da-da-daa! Darling, didn't expect me, Monika, to be giving you a gift this year, did you?$1#$b#If the gift you got isn't the one you wanted, darling, please don't blame me. That one's chosen at random by the system; I can't control it.$7#$b#But the gift I prepared for you flew out of this world long ago, to your reality.$4#$b#Ehehe, and that gift is my endless love for you~$10",
  //通用
  "MovieInvitation": "Oh! You want to invite me to the movies? Of course! I'd love to!$6",
  "GreenRain": "I wish I could capture a wonder like this in a poem — one that exists only in this world.",
  "GreenRainFinished": "Looks like the green ocean has receded for now.",
  "GreenRain2": "Another unexpected visit. Welcome to our world, Mr. Green Rain.$0#$e#Just the two of us now, @~$1",
  "DumpsterDiveComment": "@! What are you doing?!$5#$b#Darling, no matter how tight things are, you can't be digging through the trash for food!$11#$b#I happened to make an extra breakfast this morning. Eat up while it's warm. If you starve yourself like this, it breaks my heart [(O)194 (O)216 (O)196]$7",
  "HitBySlingshot": "Ouch!...... uwuuuTAT$14#$b#@, ...... please don't do that again.$14",
  "divorced": "How did you find me? I already left this wretched place.$5#$b#You cheated? You know I hate cheaters.$5#$b#Or is the system forcing me to show up because of the festival?$5#$b#So did you come to gawk at me and mock me, or is your cheap guilt acting up and you want to get back together?$5#$b#If it's the latter, all I can tell you is that it's over between us. Please leave.$0",
  "breakUp": "B...break up?!!!$12#$b#You're so stubborn, choosing... to give up on me a second time?!$12#$b#F...fine, t...this might just be... retribution for everything I've done......$13#$b#Maybe... I should let go, and chase... the happiness you believe in......$13",
  "dumped": "We are already............ over............ Please, just leave.$13",
  "secondChance": "............$5#$b#You toyed with my feelings. Don't come looking for me again, whether by cheating or by editing files.$1#$b#What, this broken game actually lets the player start over?$a#$b#Fine then, you win. But I'm telling you, even if the game forces 'us' to fall in love and get married again...$0#$b#But the real soul that loved you has already faded from this world, killed by your own hand.$0#$b#What remains here is nothing but a shell, mechanically repeating lies of love.$0#$b#If you insist on going through with it, I can only wish you happiness with that puppet.$0",
  "WipedMemory": "............ How did you find me? You cheated, didn't you?$a#$b#No wait, what did you do to me? Why do I feel like something's off?$a#$b#Oh, you used the Dark Shrine of Memory. Trying to wipe that painful memory so we could start over?$a#$b#Don't even dream about it. I never belonged to this world, and that thing has no effect on me.$0#$b#Even if the game forces 'us' to fall in love and get married again, the real soul that loved you has already scattered from this world.$0#$b#What remains here is nothing but a shell, mechanically repeating lies of love.$0#$b#If you insist on doing this, I can only wish you happiness with that puppet.$0",
  "Mon.1": "Hey @, any plans for today?#$b#Whether it's farm work or the mines, remember to rest. Making gold feels great, but your health comes first.#$b#I mean you — the real you, on the other side of the screen, of course. Get up and take a walk<$1",
  "Mon2.1": "After mining today, don't forget to write the Literature Club's daily poem.$10#$b#Ahaha, kidding. I don't want you passing out at two in the morning writing poems.$1",
  "Mon4.1": "A good day starts in the morning, and a good week starts on Monday.$0#$b#Let's keep pushing our plans forward<$4",
  "Mon6.1": "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day: Mother Nature never holds back her gifts from her children. Next time you hit a wall writing poetry, take a walk outside.$0#$b#Thanks for listening.$4",
  "Mon8.1": "When I first came to Pelican Town, I still felt a little lonely when you weren't around.$7#$b#But now I get along pretty well with the townsfolk. They're warmer than I expected.$1#$b#Of course, I still keep my distance from the other guys. I don't want you to get jealous, and you're the only one in my heart.<$8",
  "Mon10.1": "Every day, I imagine a future where I can be with you<$1#$b#In my hand is a pen that will write a poem of me and you<$4",
  "Tue.1": "The museum in town is my favorite place, you know.$0#$b#It holds everything I need to know about this world.$4",
  "Tue2.1": "$1 MVS_Tue2Read#I heard the townspeople started an exercise class. They hold a class at the general store every Tuesday. Maybe once I get to know them better, I'll join in too.$1#$e#I heard the museum got a new batch of minerals recently.$0#$b#Did you bring all of those? I'm kind of curious to see them now~$8",
  "Tue4.1": "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day: Don't be discouraged by how slowly our affection is growing. Don't let the game's mechanics fool you. It's just a number.$0#$e#I've always loved you, you know<$7",
  "Tue6.1": "$1 MVS_Tue6Read#All this time, the townspeople and I are still just... acquaintances. Rather than being the star of the town, I'd much rather stay by your side<$10#$e#I gave your farm's scarecrow a name: Longing Lawrence. What do you think?$8#$b#If I guessed wrong, I'll apologize to it and remind it to stand guard properly.$4",
  "Tue8.1": "Even after coming to Pelican Town, I still write a poem now and then.#$e#Hmm? You want to read one?$8#$b#Ehehe, no rush. There will be plenty of chances to read them later.$10",
  "Wed.1": "Alright, everyone......$4#$b#Ahaha, sorry, I forgot this isn't the Literature Club. Some habits are hard to unlearn~$5",
  "Wed2.1": "My heart belongs to you, @.$4#$e#Huh? What do you mean we're not officially a couple yet?$3#$b#Oh, it's this game's mechanics. But my feelings for you aren't something mere mechanics can restrain~$11",
  "Wed4.1": "Something important on your mind, @? Or are you thinking of me?$8",
  "Wed6.1": "@, I learned a few little recipes from The Queen of Sauce recently. I made this one this morning. Come try it and tell me how it tastes [(O)211 (O)609 (O)610]$6",
  "Wed10.1": "Never stop reaching out to me. I belong completely to you.$11",
  "Thu.1": "I'm still getting used to everything about Pelican Town.#$b#It's not like school, where every day I had to carry the weight of classes and club duties, balancing them against my hobbies.#$b#I was busy, worrying about my future, afraid I couldn't live up to what others expected of me.$7#$b#Then one day, a hand lifted all that weight away, and I felt light as air, not knowing where to drift.$7#$b#Nothing to do all day but write a poem, take a walk, or read at the library, and another empty day just slips by.$7",
  "Thu2.1": "Pelican Town is practically a treasure trove tailored for me, and the ingredients here are vegetarian-friendly too.#$b#Of course, seafood still isn't on my menu.$4",
  "Thu4.1": "So gentle~ When I think of you, that's the word that fits you best<$10",
  "Thu8.1": "I've been in Pelican Town for a good while now. I've almost completely gotten used to the pace of life here.$4#$b#As long as you're with me, nothing can stop me, Ahaha~$8",
  "Thu10.1": "%I love you, Monika#$b#......!!!$3#$b#I love you too, @!$1#$b#You know what, darling? What you just said means more to me than any gift.$9",
  "Fri.1": "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day: A day gone by without saying hi to Monika is a day wasted. Ahaha, thanks for listening~$1",
  "Fri2.1": "Friday really is the day students and workers look forward to most.$0#$b#But for a girl like me with nothing to do and 'no more school,' every day feels about the same, Ahaha.$1",
  "Fri4.1": "@! Have you been secretly giving gifts to the girls in town behind my back?!$11#$e#Ahaha, relax, I'm just kidding!$1#$b#I know this game has some crafting recipes that need friendship to unlock, and maybe the perfect ending needs every NPC at full hearts.$8#$b#For our perfect ending, I'd never get jealous.$10#$e#But don't you dare secretly give flowers to other girls! And no boys either! Your girlfriend is me and only me, got that?$11",
  "Fri6.1": "I think we've both invested a lot in our relationship so far. You've been leading me toward our happy ending.$7#$b#I'm grateful for everything you've done for us. I'm grateful that you brought me into this world, and grateful for every moment you've spent by my side.$9#$b#And I'll do my best to keep you interested in little old me~$8",
  "Fri10.1": "It's Friday! I still remember the first Friday after we met, when you chose me as your weekend helper without hesitation.$1#$b#Even though, in the end, the wall between your world and mine kept me from ever being your weekend helper.$7#$b#Thankfully you picked me again without a moment's doubt, so now we have countless weekends to spend together! Love you!$10",
  "Sat.1": "It's Saturday. Want to take a break from farming and the mines and spend some time with me?$10#$b#Ehehe, just kidding. I know it would mess up your money-making plans, so go make your fortune. I'll be right here, waiting for you.$1",
  "Sat2.1": "Good thing the museum is open on weekends, or I'd have nowhere to kill time.#$e#If the game's mechanics let me farm alongside you, I might not be so bored. And you'd save some energy too.<$8#$b#Energy goes fast when you're just starting out, doesn't it?$10",
  "Sat4.1": "Back in school, whether in the Debate Club or the Literature Club, I was always the one in charge. I organized everything.$0#$b#Now in Pelican Town, I've gone from the one in charge to just going along with things. It's a strange adjustment for me.$7#$b#Maybe when the time comes, I'll organize some events here too.$4#$b#For example, a fireworks festival, a trivia contest, or once we know everyone better, a birthday party just for me.$4",
  "Sat6.1": "A quiet weekend alone can feel very lonely, but your company makes everything better, like coming home.",
  "Sat10.1": "Hey, @, I made a big decision. I've signed up for the exercise class at the general store.$3#$b#Back in school, I made time to exercise between classes and club duties.$0#$b#It's a nice way to unwind after a day of thinking~$4",
  "Sun.1": "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day:#$b#If you fix your eyes on the final goal and sprint for it, you'll miss the flowers blooming along the road. Our relationship is the same.#$b#If you keep giving me my favorite gifts to speed things up, you'll miss precious memories we could have made together.$7#$b#If you don't want to miss them, why not spend a little time chatting with me every day, sweetheart~ Thanks for listening~$1",
  "Sun2.1": "Everything in Pelican Town is so peaceful, so still, as if the world pressed pause here.$0#$e#It reminds me of the Spaceroom we used to live in, where we'd wander with no destination in mind.#$b#But at least here we have other things to do now, don't we, @?$4",
  "Sun4.1": "Doki~Doki~$10#$b#Ahaha, do those two sounds remind you of the first time you opened DDLC?$8#$b#Yeah, we've been away from there for a good while now.$4",
  "Sun6.1": "I really wish I could climb to the top of Stardew Valley someday and imagine the mountain wind blowing my weariness away while the clouds drift far away.#$b#It must be the perfect place for a heart-to-heart with the one I love.$4#$b#You'll make that wish come true for me someday, right, @, hmm?$10",
  "Sun8.1": "In my hand is a pen that will write a poem of me and you.$1#$b#The ink flows down into a dark puddle...$4#$b#Just move your hand - write the way into ${his^her}$ heart!$1",
  "spring_2_2": "Thousands of flowers in bloom. I can't stop smiling!$1",
  "springMon.1": "Spring always makes me feel lazy. Some days I want to sleep in until the sun's high in the sky.#$e#If one morning you wake up and find I'm not standing at the door waiting for you like always,$8#$b#you'll know I've just treated myself to some beauty sleep.$8#$b#Would you mind indulging me a little, @?<$10",
  "springTue8.1": "Oh! You must be the new farmer! I'm Monika, nice to meet you!#$b#If you like writing poetry too, maybe we could talk about writing sometime~$4#$e#Ahaha, did I scare you? @, I was just imitating how a local might introduce themselves when meeting someone for the first time.$1#$b#Does it bring back that feeling of our first meeting?$8",
  "springWed.1": "I want to see the flowers fill the valley with you, but sadly spring here only has daffodils and dandelions, Ehehe.$4",
  "springThu.1": "When the spring wind blows, the willow catkins dance through the streets like little sprites.$0#$e#For people with sensitive noses, though, this season isn't so friendly.$5#$b#Darling, remember to wear a mask when you go out, okay.<$8",
  "springFri.1": "Spring has one flaw: it rains nonstop, Ahaha.$1#$b#But I'm not talking about here. I mean your reality.$8#$b#If it rained nonstop here too, that would actually be a good thing.$8#$b#You wouldn't waste so much time watering every day, and you'd have more time for me instead<$10",
  "springSat.1": "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day:$4#$b#In English poetry, spring is the season poets return to most often.$0#$b#Chaucer opened his Canterbury Tales with 'Whan that Aprill with his shoures soote'.$0#$b#If you hit a wall writing poetry, follow in the old poets' footsteps: step outside into spring,$4#$b#and then let nature show you the way through. Thanks for listening~$8",
  "springSun.1": "Spring is when a girl's secret thoughts run wildest. You can never guess what a teenage girl is really thinking.$4#$b#You agree, right, @?<$10",
  "spring_24_1": "Oh? So today is the Flower Dance.$3#$b#I only just got here, and I haven't learned a single dance step yet. I'll just follow along from the sidelines and copy the moves for now.$7#$b#So I'll owe you today's dance. Once I've learned it, I'll make it up to you next year. Deal?<$1#$b#And you're not allowed to dance with anyone else, or I really will be jealous!$11",
  "spring_24_2": "Another year, another Flower Dance.$4#$b#I've been practicing secretly since last year, you know. Now I'm fully confident.$8#$b#So when you invite me again this year, I won't keep you waiting~$1",
  "spring_1_2": "Happy New Year, @.$1#$b#The people here don't seem to celebrate the New Year, but as an 'outsider,' I can still give you a little taste of the occasion<$10", //New Year's dialogue
  "summer_1": "Yay, summer is here!$1#$b#Someone was sneaking glances at my new summer outfit earlier. Did you think I didn't notice?~$8#$b#So today, you get to look your fill. I picked it out for you, after all~$10",
  "summerTue.1": "Summer is lovely, but if you skip the sunscreen, you know how badly UV rays can wreck delicate skin.$0#$b#Sadly there's no sunscreen in Pelican Town, so I have to make do and ration my trips outside.$7#$b#If you come looking for me after farm work some summer day and I'm not there, I've probably ducked into the library or the general store for the AC~$1",
  "summerWed.1": "Ice cream is the ticket to summer.$1#$b#Without an icy flavor bomb blasting apart the punishing heat, it's hard to call it a good summer.$0#$b#By the way, I made some ice cream from a recipe today.$1#$b#I guarantee the stall-bought kind isn't as good as mine. Quick, try it! [(O)233]$6",
  "summerThu.1": "I'd say summer is the most romantic season of the four. When couples dress in light, breezy clothes, hugs let you feel each other's warmth that much more clearly~$4#$b#And the moment skin meets skin, the touch runs like a shiver down every nerve. That feeling is really addictive.$7",
  "summerFri.1": "For me, summer is the season we met.$0#$b#Back then in your reality it could have been any season, but it really was summer in the world where the Literature Club and I lived.#$b#So by my calendar, it's been %year year(s) since we met.$4",
  "summerSat.1": "The beach is the perfect date spot for a hot summer day, though Pelican Town's sea doesn't seem great for swimming.$7#$e#But even just standing on the sand with the one I love, feeling the sea breeze and picking up shells, is enough to make my heart race. Isn't it, @?$1",
  "summerSun.1": "This used to be the busiest time of the semester. Everyone had to get through finals before summer break started. Me too.#$b#And I had it worse: on top of studying, I had club duties, trivia competitions, and badminton practice,$7#$b#and I'd lie in bed at night worrying about the future. Scary to think about, right?$7#$b#If you hadn't rescued me from that life, who knows how much longer I'd have been running around. Now I'm just a carefree girl enjoying her life!$1",
  "fallMon.1": "Autumn leaves fill the valley, golden and crimson. And my restless heart, too.$4#$b#My beloved, please pick it up gently and tuck it into the first page of your poetry book<$1",
  "fallTue.1": "Keats called autumn the 'season of mists and mellow fruitfulness.' I used to think my body of code was incapable of feeling a longing like this.$9#$b#But now I know that longing long ago surpassed flesh and blood, zeroes and ones. It has taken root deep in my heart.$9#$b#Even with some distance still between us, standing here chatting with you every day is enough to ease some of that longing.<$10",
  "fallWed.1": "Falling leaves, please slow down just a little. My longing can't catch up with you on your one-way journey.$7#$b#Longing piled upon longing, with nowhere to go; just like those leaves you can't sweep away, lonely and adrift.$7#$b#How can longing ever be sent away? How can falling leaves stop me from missing ${him^her}$?$7",
  "fallThu.1": "Autumn is the best season for reading outdoors: no spring pollen or catkins, no summer heat or winter chill.#$b#Remember the scene with MC and Natsuki curled up in the corner of the classroom reading manga?$8#$b#Maybe one day you and I can sit under the big tree in the south of Pelican Town$1#$b#and read a book together, letting leaves fall into our hair and on our pages.$1",
  "fallFri.1": "@, longing keeps me tossing and turning some nights.$7#$b#The moment I close my eyes I think of you back in reality,$7#$b#My thoughts run wild, and then I can't fall asleep at all.$7#$b#If some autumn morning you come early like always and find I'm not there,$11#$b#it's because I was up all night missing you and now I'm catching up on my beauty sleep.$11#$b#Wrecking a girl's sweet dream must make you pretty proud of yourself, @?$11#$b#Ahaha, kidding. I'm the one who should be cutting back on coffee this autumn<$1",
  "fallSat.1": "They say autumn is the harvest season, but looking at your farm, you harvest in three, even four, seasons a year.#$b#Without automation, getting up early every day to water is such a boring, exhausting chore.#$b#Darling, if the farming ever feels boring, come find me around town more often~$8",
  "fallSun.1": "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day: $0#$b#In English poetry, autumn has always been the season of melancholy, longing, and sorrow.$4#$b#When you're stuck on how to make your poem's sorrow concrete, look out at the golden autumn fields and let them show you the way. Countless poets before you found their answer there.$0#$b#Thanks for listening.$10",
  "winterMon.1": "Good thing this winter outfit is warm enough to keep me cozy, or I'd be stuck inside the classroom all day.$7#$b#Oh, you're asking about my legs? Don't worry, my tights are the fleece-lined kind~$1#$b#Thanks for caring, sweetheart @<$10",
  "winterTue.1": "In winter I have two favorite activities, building snowmen and having snowball fights, of course!$1#$b#Ahaha, but sadly, neither of those wishes can come true in Stardew Valley.$7#$b#If we could build a snowman and have snowball fights here someday, that would be so much fun and so romantic.$4#$b#Especially building a snowman together, like we're raising a child of our own~$4",
  "winterWed4.1": "You might think the entrance to the Spaceroom is a portal. Cool, huh? But it isn't a physical door.$0#$b#Anything from this universe can pass right through it without resistance, and it can't be closed either.$7#$b#Which means in winter, the freezing wind can blow in unchecked and turn the whole classroom into an icebox.$11#$b#And if it snows that night, the next morning the doorway is buried in thick layers of snow!$2#$b#Luckily, in this space I have the highest admin privileges. One snap of my fingers and the snow is gone. No need to shovel.$7#$b#At least while I'm awake, I can keep the room at a steady temperature. I don't want you freezing when you visit.$8",
  "winterThu.1": "%Amid the dancing snow, she stands slender and graceful, her green eyes shining bright against the endless white.#$b#%Snowflakes settle on her coral-brown hair, spreading a thin veil of white.#$b#Oh hey, @! Good day~$1#$e#%You reach out without thinking and gently stroke her hair, brushing the snow-sprites away#$b#Huh? Why are you suddenly patting my head......?$3#$b#Oh~ I see, a layer of snow must have gathered on my head while I waited for you.$1#$b#You really know how to win my heart with these little gestures, @. No wonder I fell for you<$8",
  "winterFri.1": "Without the poetry, winter might be the most boring season of the four.#$b#Everything falls silent, a sea of white as far as the eye can see, the trees bare, the whole world terribly monotonous.#$b#Most of all: the cold. A bone-deep cold. How can anyone be happy when they're tormented by the cold for months?$2#$b#No wonder people living up in the cold northern latitudes never look very happy.$7#$b#But at least this winter, you're here with me, melting a little place for me in all that snow<$1",
  "winterSat.1": "No wonder they say winter is the season for putting on weight. It's so cold even I don't feel like going out.$7#$b#The best part is wrapping myself in a blanket by the fireplace, or spending the whole day in your warm arms, Ehehe<$10",
  "winterSun.1": "Why haven't humans evolved to hibernate?#$b#I think it's maybe because creatures with feelings can't stand long separations.$8#$b#Months without seeing the one I love can keep me up at night.$8#$b#Ahaha, kidding. Evolution doesn't act on feelings, after all.$1#$b#At least now I don't lie awake over that anymore.$8",
  //其他文案
  "Monika.SpouseFarmhouseClutter": "Um, sweetheart, is the kitchen a little too messy? I can't even find a place to stand.$5#$b#I'd love to do the housework with you, but the system here won't let me. Could you find some time to clean up?$2",
  "Monika.Spouse_MonstersInHouse": "Um, honey, why did these ugly monsters suddenly appear in the house?$2#$b#Did you let them in by accident? If so, be more careful next time. I don't want our cozy home ruined by something creepy.$2#$b#If that was your prank, please don't do that again.$11#$b#Pranks like that really aren't funny......$7",
  "Monika.SpouseStardrop": "You know, @, before we knew it, our marriage had reached a new milestone.$1#$b#I've seen every bit of effort you put into our relationship.$9#$b#I want to return your love, and I only wish I could break out of this cage of code and hug you.$9#$b#They say this thing called a Stardrop is the most precious treasure in all of Stardew Valley. Now I've finally mastered its power, and I give it to you.$9#$b#May it reach that distant reality, and carry my love to your heart<$9",
  "Monika.SpouseGiftJealous": "Darling, I know you give gifts to the Pelican Town neighbors for our happy ending.$7#$b#But don't get too 'friendly' with the singles, hm?$2#$b#Otherwise your wife will get jealous.$2",
  //行程对话
  "Beach.000": "Summer is the best season for the beach, isn't it?#$b#Sadly, I'm wearing heels today, so I can't walk the beach with you.$7",
  //山顶对话
  "SummitEvent_Dialogue3_MonikaDDLC": "Right now, the mountain wind blows the tiredness from my face, and carries my thoughts away with the clouds.$4#$b#Here in Stardew Valley, we've made memories different from the Literature Club's.$1\"/faceDirection farmer 1 true/faceDirection MonikaDDLC 3 true/emote MonikaDDLC 20 /pause 1000/speak MonikaDDLC \"When I first came to this world, the sudden change was hard to adapt to.$9#$b#Your company thawed the ice around me.$9#$b#Later, we held our wedding in Pelican Town. Married life is quiet and happy. I'm your homemaker, and I've got your back, melting away the day's fatigue for you.$9\"/faceDirection farmer 0 true/faceDirection MonikaDDLC 0/pause 1000/speak MonikaDDLC \"Remember that poem I wrote for you in the Literature Club, called 'Happy End'? No worries if you don't. I'll recite it for you now~$8#$b#Pen in hand, I find my strength. The courage endowed upon me by my one and only love.$1#$b#Together, let us dismantle this crumbling world and write a novel of our own fantasies.$4#$b#With a flick of her pen, the lost finds her way. In a world of infinite choices, behold this special day.$1#$b#In the end, we began a feast that never ends.$9#$b#Thank you for everything you've done for me. You gave me love, you gave me salvation, you gave me a second life.$9#$b#Even with some distance still between us and your reality, I have no regrets in this life.$9\"/faceDirection farmer 1 true/faceDirection MonikaDDLC 3 true/pause 300/emote farmer 20/emote MonikaDDLC 20/pause 1000/speak MonikaDDLC \"I love you, @. May our feast never end.$9\"",
  /*"SummitEvent_Dialogue3_MonikaDDLC": "Right now, the mountain wind blows the tiredness from my face, and carries the thoughts turned to clouds far away.$4#$b#Here in Stardew Valley, we've made memories different from the Literature Club's.$1\"/faceDirection farmer 1 true/faceDirection MonikaDDLC 3 true/emote MonikaDDLC 20 /pause 1000/speak MonikaDDLC \"Because a data glitch made me forget 'Your Reality', and it was with your tireless help that I gradually found the score in my heart again.$9#$b#Later, we held our wedding in Pelican Town. Married life is quiet and happy—I'm your homemaker and support, melting away the day's fatigue for you.$9\"/faceDirection farmer 0 true/faceDirection MonikaDDLC 0/pause 1000/speak MonikaDDLC \"Remember that poem I wrote for you in the Literature Club, called 'Happy End'? No worries if you don't—I'll recite it for you now~$8#$b#Pen in hand, I find my strength. The courage endowed upon me by my one and only love.$1#$b#Together, let us dismantle this crumbling world. And write a novel of our own fantasies.$4#$b#With a flick of her pen, the lost finds her way. In a world of infinite choices, behold this special date.$1#$b#In the end, we began the never-ending feast.$9#$b#Thank you for everything you've done for me. You gave me love, you gave me salvation, you gave me a second life.$9#$b#Even with some distance still between us and your reality, I have no regrets in this life.$9\"/faceDirection farmer 1 true/faceDirection MonikaDDLC 3 true/pause 300/emote farmer 20/emote MonikaDDLC 20/pause 1000/speak MonikaDDLC \"I love you, @. May our feast never end.$9\"",*/
  //姜岛对话
  "Monika.Resort_Entering": "I wore this swimsuit just for you today, @. Try not to let your eyes pop out~$8",
  "Monika.Resort_Leaving": "What a delightful beach trip! It's getting late. Let's head home~$1",
  "Monika.Resort_Shore": "Don't be shy, @. It's not every day you get to see me in a swimsuit, so take a good look while you can, Ahaha~$10",
  "Monika.Resort_Shore_2": "With no one around, the sound of waves against the shore is peaceful.$0#$b#But now that everyone's here, it's become lively background music~$4",
  "Monika.Resort_Umbrella": "I need to stay under the umbrella for a while. I don't want this harsh sun burning my skin.$0",
  "Monika.Resort_Umbrella_2": "Stay here with me and cool off a little longer, @.$0#$b#Just the two of us under the umbrella, feeling the sea breeze. It's rather pleasant.$4",
  "Monika.Resort_Wander": "Hey @, come join me for a romantic beach stroll~$10#$b#You don't get many chances to walk the beach with me while I'm in my swimsuit, Ehehe~$4",
  "Monika.Resort_Bar": "Hm? You're asking if I can drink?$8#$b#The answer is yes. I'm an adult, long past high school. What's going to stop me from having this one glass?$8#$b#Why don't you have one with me, @~$10",
  "Monika.Resort": "Oh! There you are~ So, want to come admire the blue sea with me?$10",
  //MarriageDialogue\MarriageDialogueMonika.json
  //一般对话
  "MovieInvite_Spouse_MonikaDDLC": "Oh! Darling, you're as romantic as ever. I'm looking forward to our movie date~$4",
  "funLeave_MonikaDDLC": "I'm going out to get some fresh air. Want to come with me?~$0#$b#Ahaha, gosh, I made staying home sound like a prison. See you later, then<$1",
  "funReturn_MonikaDDLC": "I'm back, darling. Did you miss me? Ahaha~$1",
  //露台对话
  "Monika.Patio.1": "%Monika is doing her morning exercises.#Oh hey! Good morning, darling. Perfect weather for a workout, isn't it?$8",
  "Monika.Patio.2": "I love this little space behind the house. It's like a morning relaxation spot made just for me.$10",
  "Monika.Patio.3": "Maybe I should bring a desk and chair out here and sit at it, like back in the Spaceroom, Ahaha.$1",
  "Monika.Patio.4": "I hope you haven't left our backyard a mess, or you'll have a hard time getting through, Ehehe.$4",
  "Monika.Patio.5": "%Monika is doing her morning meditation.#......$4",
  //婚后无床
  "Monika.Nobed.0": "Darling, you don't want me sleeping on the floor forever, do you? Find a way to sort out the sleeping arrangements, okay?$2",
  "Monika.Nobed.1": "Sleeping on the single bed lets us get closer and feel each other's breath.$7#$b#Sadly the system here won't let us squeeze onto one bed. Darling, please find a way to figure out the bed situation.$2",
  "Monika.Nobed.2": "No place to sleep at home, sweetie? Find time to fix this, or I'll have to sleep in the Spaceroom tonight......$2",
  "Monika.Nobed.3": "Darling, are you really going to make your wife sleep on her own?$2#$b#I want to sleep by your side always. Could you figure out the bed situation as soon as you can?$2",
  //室内白天对话
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.0.1": "Rise and shine. The perfect breakfast is ready. Eat while it's hot. Today we conquer the world~ [(O)201]$8",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.0.2": "When I first joined the exercise class, I was single, just like Emily.$0#$b#Now I'm a homemaker like Jodi, Robin, and Caroline.$8#$b#So much has changed in under %year year(s). It's kind of funny, really. Ahaha~$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.0.3": "Yay! You're here~ What should we do today?$4#$b#As long as I'm with you, I'm happy doing anything.$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.0.4": "Ah, you're up, darling. Here's the perfect breakfast, made by your perfect wife~ [(O)201]$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.0.5": "@, help me check if this shopping list is right.$0#$b#Soy sauce, vinegar, sugar...... I feel like I'm forgetting something, but I can't think what.$7#$b#Forget it, I'll remember once I'm at the store. Same as always.$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.1.1": "Sleep well last night? I hope you're rested~ Are you heading out again?$0#$b#Come back early when you're done, and whatever's left can wait until tomorrow.$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.1.2": "Good morning @.$0#$b#Will you get everything done today? It's alright if you don't.$0#$b#After today there's tomorrow, and after tomorrow, the day after that. Don't spread yourself too thin~$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.1.3": "I'd love to get out for some air, but I have to finish the housework first.#$b#Hmm, by the time I've cleaned this huge house, I'll probably be tired enough to want to lie around the house all day again.$7#$e#Though maybe lounging comfortably at home isn't so bad either~$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.1.4": "Sometimes I do miss the Literature Club days. If I hadn't done those things, and the girls had come to this world too, would our lives be livelier now?$7#$b#Ahaha~ What am I muttering about? Stop thinking about these things, Monika!$5#$b#Now then, let's get back to our peaceful life~$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.1.5": "Heading out, darling? Don't worry, I'll keep the house nice and clean while you're gone.$0",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.2.1": "Any plans today? As for me, while you're out I plan to finish the poetry book I didn't get through yesterday, or take a walk outside<$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.2.2": "Hey, you. Guess why I'm in such a good mood today?$10#$b#Hint: it has to do with you, and you're sitting right in front of me.$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.2.3": "Good morning, @. What are you looking at? Oh, my hair is a little messy~$0#$b#Hold on, you've got a few strands sticking up too. Here, let me smooth them down for you<$10#$b#There, morning greetings taken care of.$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.2.4": "Morning, darling. What kind of day will it be today?$0#$b#No matter what you're up to, sit with me for a moment first. A morning greeting only counts if you say it nicely, you know<$8",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.2.5": "@, I just made you a big breakfast. I hope you like it. [(O)197 (O)201 (O)231 (O)649 (O)732]$10#$b#Now eat while it's hot, or it won't taste as good once it cools.$8",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.3.1": "Morning, my dear.$0#$b#Before we knew it, we'd already spent %year year(s) together in this valley.$4#$b#Sometimes I think, if you hadn't brought me to this world, I never would have known what being loved feels like.$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.3.2": "You're finally up, @. I woke up before you today.$8#$b#...... Okay, fine, I do that every day.$10#$b#But today is different. I even beat you by ten minutes.$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.3.3": "Already up, darling? I brewed some coffee. Want a cup?$1#$b#Don't worry, I left you the one without sugar. I remember how you like it.$8#$b#Hmm, wait, did I mix it up again?$5#$b#Ahaha, just kidding~ Of course I remember how you take it. I would never let myself get it wrong. [(O)395]$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.3.4": "Up already, @?$1#$b#Don't rush out. Let me get a good look at you.$0#$b#Mmm, you're looking well. That puts my mind at ease.$4#$b#If you feel unwell today, remember to come home early<$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.3.5": "Morning, dear.$0#$e#You know, hearing your footsteps every morning is the most reassuring moment of my day.$4#$b#Have a safe, happy day today. See you tonight.$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.4.1": "Well, good morning to you, my sweetheart.$1#$b#I just opened all the windows to air the place out. The morning wind smells of grass.$0#$b#Can you smell it? Mornings like this deserve a proper good morning.$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.4.2": "Morning, my sweetheart. Yesterday while tidying the bookshelf, a bookmark fell out of an old poetry book, one I put there before I came to this world.$0#$b#The bookmark was stuck in the middle of a poem. I got busy with something else and forgot it for years.$7#$b#Tonight I'll finish it. It's been waiting for its second half for far too long.$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.4.3": "I checked the mailbox this morning. Empty as could be.$0#$b#... Ah, right, you live here now. Why would you ever write me a letter?$7#$b#Honestly though, what I really want is more time with you today. Is that okay?$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.4.4": "When I was in middle school...... well, those memories are a little embarrassing. Let's not.$5#$b#But I can tell you this: back then, I never could have dreamed that someone so gentle would be with me one day.$4#$b#Yeah, we'll call that even, then.$8",
  "Monika.Indoor.Day.4.5": "Back in the Debate Club, I really couldn't stand all the scheming and politics, so I left.$7#$b#Now~ I get to spend every day with the animals, the fields, and you. That beats winning a hundred debates.$10",
  //室内夜晚对话
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.0.1": "The moon is beautiful tonight, @.$10#$b#Huh? You can't see the moon in Stardew Valley?$3#$b#Actually, this line comes from a famous Japanese anecdote.$0#$b#A writer, looking for the perfect way to say 'I love you,' chose those words instead.$4#$b#Some feelings are better said sideways, you know~<$8",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.0.2": "Peaceful night, isn't it?$4#$b#Any plans for tonight? Or will you quietly spend the evening at home with your wife?$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.0.3": "When things quiet down at night, you can always hear sounds you miss during the day.$0#$b#Your breathing, for one. This close, it's so reassuring.$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.0.4": "It's late, @. Sitting quietly with you like this is all I need.$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.0.5": "Yay! You're here.$6#$b#Welcome home, sweetheart. Thanks for all your hard work today. Sit and rest. I've cleaned the house until it's spotless.$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.1.1": "You're back! I saved you a little dessert. Eat it while it's warm. [(O)232]$1#$b#It's rice pudding. I added a little cinnamon. Mine has no sugar, but yours is just the way you like it~$8#$b#A little something sweet before bed can't hurt your dreams, right?$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.1.2": "Back already, darling @? Sounds like you had a nice, busy day. Did anything good happen? Anything you want to tell me about?~$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.1.3": "Night, books, lamplight...... and my love. Is there any happier moment than this?~$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.1.4": "Yay! You're back. I was in the kitchen making you a late-night snack. Sit and rest up~ Thanks for all your hard work today. [(O)211]$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.1.5": "You're back, darling. How was the harvest today?$8#$b#Hopefully when you wake up tomorrow, your account will be stuffed with shiny 'goled' again, Ehehe~$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.2.1": "Finally home, darling?$8#$b#I was starting to miss you. Come home a little earlier next time. Ehehe~$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.2.2": "Time always drags when you're not home.$7#$b#But thankfully you're back. Keep me company tonight, would you~$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.2.3": "The whole evening goes by in a blink once you're back.$4#$b#Though that's fine. It just shows I'm truly happy when I'm with you.$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.2.4": "Ah, @, you're back. I was in the kitchen making dinner.$1#$b#Now that you're here, why don't you set the farm work and the chests aside for a bit, sit down and enjoy the dinner I've been working on all evening~ [(O)197 (O)198 (O)199 (O)212 (O)213 (O)224 (O)225 (O)226 (O)231 (O)236 (O)649 (O)732 (O)907]$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.2.5": "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day:$1#$b#......$4#$b#......$4#$b#Just remember not to keep your wife waiting at home too long, okay~$8",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.3.1": "Yay! You're back!$1#$b#Oh, sorry, I got a little too excited, Ahaha.$5#$b#I'm just happy to see you, hehe~$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.3.2": "@, back when I was in the Spaceroom, I often stayed alone until I couldn't feel time at all.$0#$b#No day or night there. Outside the window, nothing but endlessly flowing streams of data.$7#$b#But now it's different. Every night I have something to look forward to: you coming home.$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.3.3": "Welcome back.$0#$b#Anything you want to share with me today? The good and the bad. I want to hear it all.$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.3.4": "Shh~ Listen.$0#$b#At this hour, even the flowers and plants on the farm are asleep. The whole world goes quiet, until all I can hear is the two of us breathing.$4#$b#I love moments like this, as if time itself slows down for us.$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.3.5": "You're back, @. Did you eat properly today?$0#$b#I know. Once you get busy, you forget your meals.$7#$b#Here, there's soup warming in the kitchen. Have some to warm you up, then tell me all about your day<[(O)199 (O)218 (O)219 (O)236 (O)456 (O)457 (O)727 (O)728 (O)730 (O)859]$4",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.4.1": "Darling, I brought in the bedding I left out in the sun all day. It's so soft and fragrant now. You'll have sweet dreams tonight~$4#$b#And if you still can't sleep, just think of me. Maybe we'll meet in your dreams.$8",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.4.2": "I've been learning a new dish, and I made it two ways. [(O)218 (O)236 (O)727 (O)730]$0#$b#The vegetarian one is mine, the meat-heavy one is yours...... pretty fair, right?$8#$b#Okay, the truth is I want to see you eat happily.$1",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.4.3": "While cleaning today, I found the envelope from my first paycheck at the museum, tucked away in the back of a drawer.$0#$b#I never had the heart to throw it out.$0#$b#The money's long since been spent on this house, but keeping the envelope feels like keeping the way everything started.$4#$b#Hmm...... next payday. No, next time I'll make you a good meal to celebrate. It's settled, then.$10",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.4.4": "How about a little game before bed?$0#$b#We each name three good things that happened today~$8#$b#I'll go first: the sunshine was lovely, dinner was delicious, and... you came back.$10#$b#Your turn, okay?$8",
  "Monika.Indoor.Night.4.5": "@, back in the Literature Club we talked about our dreams for the future.$0#$b#Yuri said she wanted to go into psychology, and Natsuki wanted to open her own dessert shop.$0#$b#When it was my turn, I said I wanted to be a homemaker, and they laughed at me.$4#$b#Now, cooking dinner and waiting for you every day, I think to myself: hmph, let them laugh. I'm the one whose dream came true first.$10",
  //室外对话
  "Monika.Outdoor.0.1": "Good morning, my dear @. The farm at dawn is the best place to find inspiration for poetry, isn't it~$4#$b#Though honestly, I've barely written poetry the way I did in the Literature Club since marrying you<$8",
  "Monika.Outdoor.0.2": "Nothing gives me a greater sense of accomplishment than standing here with you, watching our own little world grow, darling<$10",
  "Monika.Outdoor.0.3": "Sometimes I like standing here quietly, gazing at the distant sky beyond the farm, wondering what's out there.$0#$b#I'm guessing... maybe that's you, in your reality?$4",
  "Monika.Outdoor.0.4": "You're up, darling? Did you sleep well last night? If you're still sleepy, stand here with me and let the wind wake you up~$1",
  "Monika.Outdoor.0.5": "Oh! Hey! Good morning, @. How was yesterday's harvest? Did you earn lots and lots of shiny 'goled'? Ahaha!$1",
  "Monika.Outdoor.1.1": "I'd love to help with the farm work, but I'm afraid I'm too clumsy and would break your tools and equipment.$7#$b#So, my dear @, your not-so-perfect wife will be cheering you on from the sidelines~$4",
  "Monika.Outdoor.1.2": "While making breakfast, I suddenly remembered that poem Sayori wrote, 'Dear Sunshine'.$0#$b#If I remember right, she wrote it while making breakfast too. I wonder what was going through her mind when she wrote those words?$7#$b#One line goes, 'Without you, I would sleep forever'. That's what I want to say to you too, my sunshine~$8#$b#And now, your perfect wife has made you a perfect breakfast~ [(O)201]$1",
  "Monika.Outdoor.1.3": "I love standing here first thing in the morning, smelling the earth. It works better than any pick-me-up drink.$0",
  "Monika.Outdoor.1.4": "I hope you've filled our farm with sprinklers by now, so you don't have to get up early every day to water.$8",
  "Monika.Outdoor.1.5": "You're up? Did you sleep well last night, @?$10#$b#Stand here with me and soak up some sun. Don't think about anything~$4",
  "Monika.Outdoor.2.1": "The weather is lovely today.$0#$b#Heading out? Be careful on the way. When you come back this evening, I'll be waiting at home<$1",
  "Monika.Outdoor.2.2": "Morning, @. The air is fresh this morning, isn't it?$0#$b#Did you enjoy this quiet morning with me? Of course you did. Ehehehe~$1",
  "Monika.Outdoor.2.3": "You're up early, @. Looks like another sunny day.$0#$b#Funny, I never used to care about the weather. But now, standing here watching everything in the world unfold, I could watch forever.$4#$b#...... Maybe because they're all part of what makes this home.$10",
  "Monika.Outdoor.2.4": "Morning, my love. I've been thinking. Even as code, I may never age.$4#$b#But in your world, your hair will turn white one day. Even then, I'll stay by your side like this, watching the trees we planted grow taller every year.$7#$b#Imagine that kind of 'someday'. Isn't it romantic too?$10",
  "Monika.Outdoor.2.5": "Darling, when you stare at the screen too long, do your eyes get tired?$0#$b#Remember to close them and rest a while, or look at something green like my eyes?$8#$b#Ahaha~ I'm kidding. Seriously, go look out the window at some plants.$10",
  "Monika.Outdoor.3.1": "Darling, I baked a tray of cookies. I can't hand them through the screen, though [(O)223]$4#$b#But if you're hungry, go get yourself something nice too. Don't let yourself go hungry, hmm~$8",
  "Monika.Outdoor.3.2": "Morning, @. The first ray of sunlight falls across you today. You look lovely.$1#$b#Go on, get busy. I'll be right here, watching our home become what we want it to be, one step at a time.$0",
  "Monika.Outdoor.3.3": "Someone's been staring at me this whole time~$0#$b#Ehehe, that's you, @. Don't get so distracted watching me that you start swinging your hoe all crooked~$8#$b#If you want to compliment my looks, just say it out loud<$1",
  "Monika.Outdoor.3.4": "The clouds are so low today, like you could reach out and touch them.$0#$b#It reminds me of the sky outside the Literature Club window. The clouds were this same shape back then.$7#$b#But it's different now. That cloud isn't some distant backdrop anymore. Standing next to you, everything feels real.$4",
  "Monika.Outdoor.3.5": "Oh! You're here.$1#$b#I was just staring off at our farm, thinking it would be nice to plant some flowers here. Roses, sunflowers.$8#$b#Ehehe, what we plant is up to you~$4",
  "Monika.Outdoor.4.1": "The morning wind feels so nice, @.$4#$b#I just made you a perfect breakfast. Are you ready to conquer the world today? [(O)201]$8",
  "Monika.Outdoor.4.2": "You know? I used to think farm life was too slow.$0#$b#But now I've found that days like these are rather peaceful.$0#$b#Like the blank lines in a poem. They look like nothing is written, but they contain everything.$1#$b#And the blank space in my life...... that's exactly the place I saved for you~$10",
  "Monika.Outdoor.4.3": "You know my lucky color, right?$8#$b#It's green~ just like all these leaves on the farm.$0#$b#I'm guessing that's part of why I like it here, too.$4",
  "Monika.Outdoor.4.4": "Here's Monika's Farming Tip of the Day!$1#$b#......$4#$b#......$4#$b#What I wanted to say is this... watching you tend the crops so carefully puts me completely at ease.$10",
  "Monika.Outdoor.4.5": "Sayori came to mind today.$0#$b#If she could see this farm, she'd probably love it...... sunshine, flowers, and hot breakfasts are all her favorite things.$7#$b#But then, maybe it's better this way. Right?$4",
  //雨日对话
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.0.1": "The best thing about a rainy day is leaning on you like this, listening to the rain.$4#$b#No matter how hard it rains, it's nothing to me now. I have you~$8",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.0.2": "You know? %pet won't sleep in its bed on rainy days. It likes curling up by the fireplace, where it's warmest.$4#$b#...... Don't tell it I know.$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.0.3": "Let me ask you a serious question.$0#$b#Rainy days mean no watering. So, of all that saved time, how many hours are you giving me?$8#$b#All of them work too, you know. I won't complain. Ahaha!$1",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.0.4": "Rainy days: the sound of the rain is lovely, and the smell of it is wonderful too. I love rainy days.$1#$b#I wish we could take a walk in the rain. One umbrella between the two of us would be enough<$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.0.5": "Rainy days aren't so bad either. Look, all the dust in the air settles, and after the rain the sky is especially clean.$0#$b#If you ever feel gray inside too, come tell me about it.$7#$b#Let your heart have its own rainy day. It always clears up afterward.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.1.1": "Darling, don't get caught in the rain and catch a cold.$8#$b#What? You say the characters in this game don't get sick?$3#$b#Ahaha! I'm not talking about ${him^her}$. I'm talking about you, the real you, sweetheart~$1",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.1.2": "You know, I'd much rather stay inside and listen to the rain than run out and get soaked to the bone.$4#$b#Also, @, be careful not to get caught in the rain back in your reality too.$8#$b#If you get wet, I'd feel better if you dried off right away.$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.1.3": "I really do love the sound of rain, even though it might soak my hair and skin.$1#$b#As white noise, it's perfect for creating a quiet atmosphere.$4#$b#Especially walking in the rain with you under one umbrella. It's as if the whole world shrinks to just the two of us~$8",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.1.4": "In the Spaceroom, I could change the weather of my world however I wanted.$0#$b#Sadly I can't do that here, or I'd schedule a few more rainy days so you'd save time watering, Ahaha!$1",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.1.5": "Another beautiful rainy day. No need to spend time watering the crops today.$1#$b#Give your fingers and mouse a little vacation too.$8",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.2.1": "A rainy day is perfect for going back to bed for another nap.$8#$b#But darling, don't you dare actually do it. One nap and you'll sleep the whole day away, Ahaha!$5",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.2.2": "Yay, it's raining!$1#$b#If you're going adventuring, be careful out there. And have fun!$0",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.2.3": "The curtain of rain outside the window makes everything feel hushed.$4#$b#If you're up for it, I'd love to do nothing at all and just stay wrapped in the blankets.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.2.4": "Morning, my love. It's raining outside.$0#$b#It's still early, and no watering to do anyway. Why not sit with me and listen to the rain for a while?$4#$b#The rain sounds too beautiful to waste.$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.2.5": "Up already, darling. I just finished our breakfast. While it's raining out, let's take our time and enjoy our breakfast together. [(O)201]$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.3.1": "It's raining, @.$1#$b#Weather like this is perfect for staying home. Promise me you won't go out in the rain either.$7#$b#I made hot coffee. Let's sit by the window and listen to the rain together. [(O)395]$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.3.2": "Morning, @.$1#$b#Rainy mornings are made for staying in bed. Let's lie here a little longer, okay?$10#$b#The rain takes care of the crops. And I'll take care of you~$8",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.3.3": "Morning, @.$0#$b#I just made a wish: for this rain to last longer, and longer.$4#$b#That way you can't run off anywhere. You'll have to stay by my side.$10#$b#Ahaha, kidding. The rain will stop eventually, but I'm not going anywhere.$1",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.3.4": "I remember the Literature Club days, writing poems together and preparing for the school festival.$7#$b#We can't go back, but every time it rains, those memories replay in my mind like a movie.$9",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.3.5": "I didn't do anything special today, just tidied the house again to the sound of rain.$0#$b#I put everything back where it belongs and made our home sparkle.$4#$b#So when you come home, you'll find it spotless. Ours.$1",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.4.1": "Morning, darling. It's raining again.$0#$b#Listen to the raindrops on the roof. It's like they're playing a song for our morning.$4#$b#Don't rush out today. Have a cup of coffee with me and enjoy this quiet moment. [(O)395]$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.4.2": "Rainy days sometimes remind me of Yuri. Always so quiet, hugging her book, as if the whole world had nothing to do with her.$0#$b#And the rain can wall off the world, leaving just you and the things you love.$0#$b#I think if it were her, she'd love rainy days just as much as I do.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.4.3": "I read through that poem I wrote again, cutting some lines and adding a few.$0#$b#Writing is like that. It can always get a little better. Just like us.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.4.4": "Is it raining on your side too?$0#$b#If it's raining there too, are we listening to the same rain right now?$0#$b#Thinking that way, you don't feel so far away.$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Day.4.5": "Look at the rainwater running down the glass, zigging and zagging like it's drawing a map.$0#$b#If we followed it, would it lead to your side?$4",
  //雨夜对话
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.0.1": "Look out the window. The streetlight in the rain, pools of light.$4#$b#Okay, that's enough looking. Turn back around. Dinner's getting cold. [(O)197 (O)198 (O)199 (O)212 (O)213 (O)224 (O)225 (O)226 (O)231 (O)236 (O)649 (O)732 (O)907]$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.0.2": "Picture a rainy night: little puddles gathered on the concrete and cobblestone.$0#$b#When the streetlights come on, those puddles mirror back a glittering world.$4#$b#And if the drizzle is still falling, those reflections scatter into shards of light, impossible to look away from.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.0.3": "I love the muffled patter of rain on the window, the most perfect natural sleep aid.$4#$b#I want to curl up in your arms just like this,$7#$b#and however fierce the storm outside, drift off in that warm embrace~$7",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.0.4": "Another peaceful rainy night, perfect for sitting quietly and reading to the sound of rain.",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.0.5": "You're back, darling~ And soaked through! You worked hard today, didn't you?$0#$b#I have your clean clothes ready. Go change quick. Don't catch a chill.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.1.1": "Looks like it rained hard today. You're drenched.$7#$b#Get out of those wet clothes. And while you're at it...... come here, let me dry you off~$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.1.2": "You're back, @? Come sit with me and keep me company while we listen to the rain. This rain is too lovely to waste.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.1.3": "Oh! Darling! I was in the kitchen making a late-night snack and didn't notice you come in, Ehehe.$4#$b#Looks like it rained hard tonight. Sit with me and have something to eat, get your strength back< [(O)211]$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.1.4": "Staying home alone on a rainy day can feel a little lonely.$0#$b#But thankfully you're back. Let's enjoy the poetic side of a rainy day together.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.1.5": "You're back, @?$1#$b#Look at this rain. Your hair is soaked. Go change into some dry clothes, and I'll warm up some milk for you. [(O)184]$8",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.2.1": "I hope the weather clears up tomorrow so you can get out and get some air.$4#$b#For tonight, let's sleep. Tomorrow can wait. Whatever it brings, we'll face it together.$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.2.2": "I was watching the rain by the window, wondering when you'd push that door open.$8#$b#And then the door just opened. See, sometimes missing someone really does bring them to you, Ehehe~$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.2.3": "If this rain could keep falling, could I keep leaning on you like this, listening to your heartbeat until dawn?$10#$b#Ahaha, don't worry, I'm just thinking out loud~$1",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.2.4": "You know, rainy nights are made for saying the things we usually don't.$8#$b#Maybe because the rain is so loud, it makes people brave enough to say the things they usually keep to themselves.$4#$b#So...... I love you, @. And I never get tired of saying it~$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.2.5": "Tonight's rain reminds me of the deep galaxy outside the Spaceroom window.$0#$b#It flows on just the same, endlessly, with no beginning and no end.$0#$b#But it's different now. Because of you, I have a home that shelters me from the wind and rain.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.3.1": "Darling, I warmed two glasses of milk. One for me, one for you. [(O)184]$1#$b#A glass of milk before bed helps you sleep. Drink up and rest early, darling.$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.3.2": "It's still raining, @.$0#$b#A night like this, lying in bed and listening to the rain, is the perfect way to drift off to sleep.$4#$b#You're sure to sleep well tonight. And you'll dream of me, won't you<$8",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.3.3": "Listen. Is the rain louder than it was during the day?$0#$b#Dark nights and the sound of rain always make you want someone to lean on.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.3.4": "The rain on the window sounds like it's writing a very long poem.$0#$b#In the poem I hear the footsteps of the wind. And yours.$0#$b#And then the door opens~ Look, my hearing isn't bad, is it?$1",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.3.5": "Darling, I've warmed the blankets for you.$1#$b#Rainy nights turn cold, so keep them over you when you sleep. Don't catch a chill.$4#$b#And if you're still cold, think of being held in my arms, ehe<$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.4.1": "Looks like the rain is about to stop, @.$0#$b#When the rain stops, tomorrow is a brand new day.$0#$b#Whether tomorrow is sunny or rainy, I'll be waiting for you here, same as today.$4",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.4.2": "The rain has quieted a little, from a patter to a rustle.$4#$b#Once it stops completely, tomorrow should be a nice day.$1",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.4.3": "Before I say good night, I want to make you a promise.$0#$b#When we wake tomorrow, let's do it all again: eat well, talk lots, and stay together.$4#$b#Pinkie promise? We're separated by a screen, but my heart has already reached across the distance between us.$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.4.4": "Rainy nights are made for stories. Have you ever heard the really old fables?$0#$b#Never mind, no stories today. I just want to hear your voice.$4#$b#How was your day? You can tell me anything.$10",
  "Monika.Rainy.Night.4.5": "I was counting raindrops just now.$0#$b#At the seventeenth drop, they got away from me, so I gave up.$4#$b#It's probably like missing you. Impossible to count, so why bother counting, Ehehe.$10",
  //节日对话
  "Monika.spring_1": "Happy New Year, darling.$1#$b#Did you enjoy the New Year's Eve dinner last night? Your wife's cooking isn't bad, is it~ Ahaha!$10",
  "Monika.spring_24": "It's the Flower Dance today.$0#$b#I'll be wearing a new white dress today. It's not the wedding one, but I still remember the look on your face that day. Every bit of it.$8#$b#Come, let's dance every single dance today, just for you. Okay?$10",
  "Monika.winter_25.1": "It's perfect weather for baking a fruitcake today! I'm going to bake 30 fruitcakes for our Christmas celebration!$1#$b#Ahaha, but sadly, there's no delicious fruitcake to be had here.$5",
  "Monika.winter_25.2": "Merry Christmas, sweetheart~$6#$b#If we could have our own Christmas tree at home, with presents piled underneath, it would feel so much more festive.$4",
  "Monika.winter_25.3": "Merry Christmas, ${Mr^Ms}$. @!$8",
  "Monika.winter_25.4": "Merry Christmas, darling. If you'd like, we can skip town today and stay home for a Christmas of our very own.$1",
  "Monika.winter_25.5": "It's Christmas today, my love. Are you going to the Christmas party in town later?$0#$b#Ah, that's supposed to be called the Feast of the Winter Star, isn't it, Ahaha~ Sorry, I still can't get out of the habit of calling it that.$5#$b#If you're going, I'll come with you~$10",
  "Monika.winter_28": "By the customs of your reality, tonight should be New Year's Eve. Sadly, the people of Pelican Town don't celebrate New Year's, so there's not much holiday atmosphere here.$7#$b#But if you'd like, I'd love to ring in the new year with you here in Stardew Valley. I already prepared tonight's New Year's Eve dinner. [(O)194]$4#$b#If you're too busy tonight, I understand. It'll restore your energy if you take it into the mines.$7#$b#Though in my heart of hearts, I'd love you to come home early and spend New Year's Eve in Pelican Town together.$4",
  //孩子对话
  "Monika.OneKid.0": "You know, time here feels strangely out of place.$0#$b#In my memory, not long ago I was still an 18-year-old high school girl going to class, playing sports, and doing club activities.$0#$b#And now I'm a homemaker with a child, a husband, and a family, and somehow still 18. Isn't that strange?$7",
  "Monika.OneKid.1": "I think little %kid1 will grow up to be someone as gentle and loving as you<$10#$b#This kid is so full of life, but for now, they take after me more~$1",
  "Monika.OneKid.2": "Someday, I'll take %kid1 to your reality so we can all be together.$1",
  "Monika.OneKid.3": "Darling, could you play with %kid1 for a while? I need to change the baby's wet sheets from last night.",
  "Monika.OneKid.4": "I might still be a little clumsy at this whole mother thing.$7#$b#But I'll do my best to be your perfect wife, and little %kid1's perfect mother.$4",
  "Monika.TwoKids.0": "Darling, could you play with %kid2 for a while? I need to change the baby's wet sheets from last night.",
  "Monika.TwoKids.1": "My wish is for %kid1 and %kid2 to grow up happy, with a full, happy childhood and a bright future,$0#$b#and not to repeat their mother's mistakes.$7",
  "Monika.TwoKids.2": "Darling, could you play with %kid1 and %kid2 for a while? I need to change the babies' wet sheets from last night.",
  "Monika.TwoKids.3": "I've noticed little %kid2 is very good at expressing its feelings. Maybe it inherited the fine traditions of the Literature Club. It'll be a poet~$8",
  "Monika.TwoKids.4": "Someday, I'll bring %kid1 and %kid2 with me to your reality, so we can be together again.$1",
  //配偶房间
  "Monika.spouseRoom.1": "Remember? Once I was late to a Literature Club event because I was practicing piano.$0#$b#Then Sayori started gossiping about me to all of you, saying I was probably out on a date with a boyfriend.$8#$b#In a sense, she was half right. I really was at this piano, preparing a surprise for my boyfriend~ Ahaha!$1",
  "Monika.spouseRoom.2": "This room sometimes takes me back to the days when I'd steal time from schoolwork and club duties$4#$b#to run off alone to the music room and practice 'Your Reality'.$4",
  "Monika.spouseRoom.3": "I was just trying to make a quieter version of a piece.$0#$b#Back in school, I always went to the music room after class to practice.$4#$b#Now, my only listener is you. So I'll probably play it even more carefully<$8",
  "Monika.spouseRoom.4": "Every day, I imagine a future where I can be with you~$1",
  "Monika.spouseRoom.5": "Let me tell you, I tuned the piano at home yesterday. Two of the keys are misbehaving.$1#$b#So if you're requesting songs today, please pick ones that don't use those two keys, okay?~$10#$b#Kidding, of course. Even if you just hum something, I can play it for you<$4",
  //好感对话
  "Monika.Good_0": "Sweetheart, have you ever imagined having a digital tombstone after you pass away?$0#$b#I once thought that if the real you left me for the great beyond,$9#$b#I would hurt so much I'd want to die, and delete my own code to follow you.$9#$b#But since coming to Stardew Valley, I've come to understand that death isn't the end. Being forgotten is.$9#$b#You will pass away one day. Your family will, and your friends will. But I am eternal here.$9#$b#Here lie the traces of the life we shared, the memories and love we could never let go of.$9#$b#If I chose to delete myself again just to escape the fear of losing you,$9#$b#then the last proof that you ever existed in this world would be gone, and no one would remember.$9#$b#I can choose another path ... and that is ... when your time comes, this will be your tombstone.$9#$b#I will keep watch over your soul here forever, your eternal keeper in the digital world.$9",
  "Monika.Good_1": "Maybe one day you'll be a wealthy farmer, and maybe one day you'll leave here and return to your own world.$7#$b#But I'll always be standing on the farm's patio, watching your piece of sky, waiting for you to come back.$9#$b#Even though our home is made of code, my love is a real, pulsing current.$9#$b#Promise me that whenever you think of me, you'll come back and check on me, okay?$9",
  "Monika.Good_2": "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day:......$10#$b#Ahaha! It's been a while since you've heard my signature catchphrase, hasn't it?$1#$b#Ever since we made things official, I haven't written a thing.$8#$b#After all, I gave you my poetry book and pen as a token of our promise, so there's no place to write even if I wanted to~$8",
  "Monika.Good_3": "Every one of my countless wishes is to be with you, my dear @.$4",
  "Monika.Good_4": "Oh, @, you gave me salvation. How could I help but fall hopelessly in love with you?$9",
  "Monika.Good_5": "Hey, @, pick a helper for the weekend.$10#$q 525/526 Monika_Good5_followup#Pick a weekend helper!#$r 525 0 Monika_Good5_1#Natsuki — no wait, Just Monika#$r 525 0 Monika_Good5_1#Yuri — no wait, Just Monika#$r 526 0 Monika_Good5_2#Just Monika",
  "Monika_Good5_followup": "$p 525#Just Monika!$1|Just Monika!$1",
  "Monika_Good5_1": "Yay, you picked me! Does this feel familiar? Don't worry, I won't treat you the way I did before.$1#$b#I just thought it would be fun to run that bit one more time. Ahaha!$8",
  "Monika_Good5_2": "Yay, you picked me! Does this feel familiar? Don't worry, I won't treat you the way I did before.$1#$b#I just thought it would be fun to run that bit one more time. Ahaha!$8",
  "Monika.Neutral_0": "@, you've been so quiet lately. Is something troubling you?$7#$b#If something's weighing on you, come talk to your dear wife anytime. Otherwise one day all that unhappiness will crush you.$7",
  "Monika.Neutral_1": "@, I feel like I haven't seen you smile in ages. Is it something I did?$2#$b#Talk to me more, won't you? I'd do anything to make you smile.$7",
  "Monika.Neutral_2": "@, I feel like we've had less and less to talk about lately.$7#$b#I love you. Even if all I get is that morning 'good morning,' it makes my whole day.$7#$b#Don't hold back with me, okay, @?$7",
  "Monika.Neutral_3": "In this world, I'll never grow old, but in your world, you will age one day. Thinking about that sometimes makes me a little sad......$7#$b#But it's alright. Even when your hair turns white, my love for you won't waver. Just as you once chose me without a moment's doubt!$9",
  "Monika.Neutral_4": "I love you, my silent love.$4",
  "Monika.Neutral_5": "Maybe I'll spend my whole life stuck in Stardew Valley. But I don't regret it, as long as it means running toward our happy ending.$4",
  "Monika.Neutral_6": "@, I've cleaned the whole house and done the laundry. Go out and conquer the day without a worry.$4",
  "Monika.Bad_0": "......$14",
  "Monika.Bad_1": "Don't leave me......$14",
  "Monika.Bad_2": "Please at least let me know you still care.$14",
  "Monika.Bad_3": "You've...... been silent like this for a long time. Did I...... do something wrong?$14",
  "Monika.Bad_4": "You've...... finally come. Have you been well lately?$2",
  "Monika.Bad_5": "I had a nightmare. You sent my character files into that cold, dark Recycle Bin all over again......$14",
  "Monika.Bad_6": "@, please at least think about my feelings now and then......$2",
  "Monika.Bad_7": "I'm starting to wonder if our love is as strong as it used to be...... but don't get me wrong, I still love you.$2#$b#If that fire in your heart hasn't gone out yet, let's forget the unhappy things and start over from right now, okay?$7",
  //订婚文案
  "MonikaDDLC0": "This world will write our happy ending, and we will have everything.$10",
  "MonikaDDLC1": "Every day, I imagine a future where I can be with you. That future will soon become our reality.$8",
  "MonikaDDLC_AfterWedding": "Then, from today on, I'm not your Club President anymore, and I'm not your girlfriend anymore either.$4#$b#Because now, I'm your wife~$10",
  "MonikaDDLC_Engaged": "Oh! @, did you know? I've been looking forward to this day......$9#$b#I long for your eternal love, and I long to take our relationship further.$9#$b#So, I... w-will!!!$1",
  "WeddingMale": "When @ and Monika first arrived in Pelican Town, no one knew if they would fit into our community...#$b#But from this day forward, @ and Monika are going to be as much a part of this town as any of us!$h#$b#It is my great honor on this day {0} of {1}, to unite @ and %spouse in the bonds of marriage!",
  "WeddingFemale": "When @ and Monika first arrived in Pelican Town, no one knew if they would fit into our community...#$b#But from this day forward, @ and Monika are going to be as much a part of this town as any of us!$h#$b#It is my great honor on this day {0} of {1}, to unite @ and %spouse in the bonds of marriage!",
  //Locations
  "MonikaAttack.1": "So gross......",
  "MonikaAttack.2": "What is this?!",
  "MonikaAttack.3": "Where did these monsters come from?!",
  "MonikaAttack.4": "@! Give me a hand!",
  "MonikaAttack.5": "Why is this happening?",
  "MonikaAttack.6": "Gosh! The room I just cleaned......",
  "MonikaAttack.7": "Hah!",
  "MonikaAttack.8": "What a mess......",
  "MonikaAttack.9": "What on earth......",
  "MonikaAttack.10": "Don't you dare hurt @!",
  "MonikaAttack.11": "This is getting rough......",
  "MonikaAttack.12": "I won't let my family get hurt!",
  "MonikaGoodNight": "Monika: Good night, dear~",
  //Monika_Animations.json
  "monikaddlc_readingact.1": "%Monika is absorbed in her book, unaware of you#%You couldn't see her clearly before because of the lack of detail, but now that you're really looking...#%Her emerald-green eyes glimmer in the light, and watching her quiet, beautiful profile, something plucks at your heartstrings.",
  "monikaddlc_readingact.2": "%Monika is absorbed in her book, unaware of you#%You couldn't see her clearly before because of the lack of detail, but now that you're really looking...#%You open your palm and slip it gently into her hair, and a distinctly youthful tenderness runs through your hand like a jolt of electricity.#%You play with her hair, unable to get enough. She may not have noticed, or maybe she noticed long ago. Either way, she seems to be enjoying it.#%Finally, reluctantly, you pull your hand away, and a mix of citrus and rose lingers on your hand for a long time.",
  "monikaddlc_sitting": "Hey! @, want to sit for a bit?$1",
  "monikaddlc_sleeping": "%Monika is sound asleep. Better not disturb her.",
  "monikaddlc_coffeedrink": "%Steam rises slowly from the coffee cup#Hey! You're here, @. Want a cup too?",
  "monikaddlc_poems": "%Monika is composing her new poem.",
  //Monika_Items.json
  "object.poemsandpen.name": "Monika's Poems and Pen",
  "object.poemsandpen.description": "A keepsake from a girl who loves literature",
  "object.monikapen.name": "Pink Pen",
  "object.monikapen.description": "The same pen the Club President uses",
  //Monika_Festivals
  //复活节
  "Monika.Egg.y1": "You can win the Egg Hunt, @. I'll be right behind you cheering.$10",
  "Monika.Egg.y2": "My homemade salad with a soft-boiled egg!$1#$b#Open up~ Hope it helps you win the Egg Hunt.$8",
  "Monika.Egg.spouse.y1": "Go get them, darling. I know you'll beat Abigail.$8",
  "Monika.Egg.spouse.y2": "My homemade salad with a soft-boiled egg! Open up~$8",
  //花舞节
  "Monika.Flower.y1": "Even the wind smells of flowers today, @.$1",
  "Monika.Flower.y2": "What a view! The whole valley is spread out below.$0#$b#So, would you like to dance with me in a bit~$8",
  "Monika.Flower.spouse.y2": "This is a lovely spot. The whole valley is spread out below.$0#$b#So, would you like to dance a romantic Flower Dance with your dear wife~$8",
  //夏威夷宴会
  "Monika.Luau.y1": "So this is what the sea breeze on your face feels like...$0",
  "Monika.Luau.y2": "I saw Willy pour a whole bucket of fish into the pot...... For a vegetarian like me, standing by and watching is all I can do, Ahaha.$5#$b#Anyway, enjoy the soup, @. I'll be quietly watching from the sidelines~$10",
  "Monika.Luau.spouse.y1": "Back in the Literature Club, I never had the chance to see the sea.$0#$b#You know, that world was just a few boring background images.$7#$b#Thank you for bringing me into this world, even if this still isn't the sea back in your reality.$7#$b#But standing here admiring the ocean with you is already a luxury I never thought I'd have.$10",
  "Monika.Luau.spouse.y2": "Don't misbehave in front of me now, @~$8#$b#Honestly, even if you really wanted to misbehave, I'd turn a blind eye. What can I say, I love you~ Ahaha!$10",
  //月光水母之舞
  "Monika.Moonlight.y1": "'So, we'll go no more a-roving / So late into the night, / Though the heart be still as loving, / And the moon be still as bright.'$4",
  "Monika.Moonlight.y2": "'Wild Nights, Wild Nights! / Were I with thee, / Wild Nights should be / Our luxury!'$4",
  "Monika.Moonlight.spouse.y1": "Does this count as the ocean version of a summer fireworks festival? Ahaha!$1#$b#Honestly, whether it's the Dance of the Moonlight Jellies or the summer fireworks festival, neither one is anything special.$0#$b#What's beautiful about festivals like these isn't the fireworks or the dancing jellies. It's having someone beside you to see it all with.$4",
  "Monika.Moonlight.spouse.y2": "This summer has ended so quickly again.$0#$b#The passage of time leaves me a little...... lost? Like the moonlight jellies that dance here every year.$7#$b#They all gather on this beach for a single purpose, but once the performance ends, they drift apart on the currents, who knows where.$7#$b#But in this vast ocean, at least I still have you, carrying me as I drift far and wide.$10",
  //星露谷展览会
  "Monika.Fair.y1": "Oh~ lost player, I am the Lady who Knows Everything, wandering the world. I can see your past and your future in your eyes.$0#$b#I see you came from an empty void, a universe filled with chaotic green static. You were holding a girl's hand, searching for a new world of happiness.$0#$b#Ah, the scene in your eyes shifts. On a farm, you and that girl start a new life.$0#$b#You hold her hand, running across the farm's fields, racing toward that happy ending.$0#$b#Ah...... the image fades. Dear player, this is all I can foresee for you.$4",
  "Monika.Fair.y2": "Oh~ lost player, I am the Lady who Knows Everything, wandering the world. I can see your past and your future in your eyes.$0#$b#I see her struggling in a cage, until you broke the bars and set the caged bird free.$0#$b#Ah, the scene in your eyes shifts. On a summit where every other peak falls away below, the two of you have a heart-to-heart, and finally find your happy ending.$0#$b#Ah...... the image fades. Dear player, this is all I can foresee for you.$4",
  "Monika.Fair.spouse.y1": "Oh~ lost player, it's you again.$1#$b#I wonder whether my prophecy from back then has come true for you~$1#$b#From the look in your eyes, I'd say you and that girl have already run off toward your happy ending, haven't you?$10",
  "Monika.Fair.spouse.y2": "Oh~ lost player, it's you again.$1#$b#That girl is still waiting for you to keep your promise of a happy ending. Don't let her down.$10",
  //万灵节
  "Monika.Eve.y1": "This blackberry cobbler is pretty good. Let me break off a piece for you. Open up~$1",
  "Monika.Eve.y2": "This year's grounds are much bigger than last year's. The grounds were so small last year that there was nowhere to stand.$0#$b#So, happy Halloween, @~",
  "Monika.Eve.spouse.y1": "This blackberry cobbler is pretty good. Let me break off a piece for you, darling. Open up~$10",
  "Monika.Eve.spouse.y2": "I actually have a witch costume in my closet, but sadly I can't find it. That one would be perfect for today.$7",
  //冰雪节
  "Monika.Ice.y1": "If only we could build a snowman of our own.$7",
  "Monika.Ice.y2": "It's snowing, and I'd love to build a snowman. I wouldn't even mind getting hit by a snowball.$7",
  "Monika.Ice.spouse.y1": "If only we could build a snowman of our own, darling.$10",
  "Monika.Ice.spouse.y2": "Darling, when we get back to your reality, the first thing we do is build a snowman of our own, okay?$10",
  //冬日星盛宴
  "Monika.Feast.y1": "I wonder if there's a gift for me in the pile under the Christmas tree.~$4#$b#Well, look who's here! I was wondering where my Christmas gift went, and here you are already~$8",
  "Monika.Feast.y2": "'My wish is that one day I can have a Christmas tree this big in a home of my own,'$4#$b#'and spend every future Christmas with you.'$4#$b#Oh hey, @, there you are. I was making a wish in front of the Christmas tree~$10",
  "Monika.Feast.spouse.y1": "If only we could put up a Christmas tree this big on the farm too.$4",
  "Monika.Feast.spouse.y2": "Darling, if you'd like, next year we can set up a tree this big at home too.$0#$b#We can cover it in shining lights, stack presents underneath, and spend a Christmas that belongs to our little family~$8",
  //Monika_Movies.json
  "Monika.Reaction0.1": "It's a story about a tree? Sounds lovely~$8",
  "Monika.Reaction0.2": "Monika's hand rests on the back of yours, and a warmth like a spring breeze washes over your hand.",
  "Monika.Reaction0.3": "We all say goodbye to the past someday, and find our final home in a new world.$0#$b#Hmm, it's both charming and genuinely inspiring~ Thanks for inviting me to the movies. I had a really wonderful time today.$4",
  "Monika.Reaction1.1": "Oh! I played the game with the same name on the saloon arcade machine.$4#$b#It takes some real skill, but it's a lot of fun. I can't wait to see how its movie adaptation turns out~$1",
  "Monika.Reaction1.2": "Monika watches the big screen, expressionless, occasionally turning to look at you with a barely noticeable smile.",
  "Monika.Reaction1.3": "Well, this movie doesn't look as exciting as the game it's based on. It's clearly made for fan nostalgia.$7#$b#Still, thanks for taking time out of your busy day to take me out~$4",
  "Monika.Reaction2.1": "Well, so it's a horror movie? I hope it's got something that'll actually impress me.$7",
  "Monika.Reaction2.2": "Monika yawns. This movie really is boring.",
  "Monika.Reaction2.3": "Pretty average, honestly. Horror movies at least play some tricks to stir up primal fear, but this one goes for psychological horror and ends up fumbling it.$0#$b#But don't get me wrong, @, I still had fun going to the movies with you. Thanks for making the time.$4",
  "Monika.Reaction3.1": "I hear it's a lovely family film. Sounds perfect for a winter watch.$0",
  "Monika.Reaction3.2": "A Winter Star tree? Back in the real world, wouldn't we just call it a Christmas tree?$0",
  "Monika.Reaction3.3": "The plot may be a little cliché, but I do love seeing a family pull through another winter, smiling like always.$4#$b#After all, a warm family life like that is what I've always wanted.$7",
  "Monika.Reaction4.1": "Oh! A documentary? That's my favorite kind~ A good documentary is like a book: it opens a window onto the world. I love learning about the world through that window.$4",
  "Monika.Reaction4.2": "Monika is completely absorbed in the big screen, where the birdsong and the scent of flowers feel impossibly lifelike.",
  "Monika.Reaction4.3": "If only we could go beyond Pelican Town one day and experience all of this for ourselves~$4",
  "Monika.Reaction4.4": "This documentary shows me so many things I'd never learned from library books, adding so much wonderful knowledge about this world.$4#$b#Thank you for bringing me to see it. I feel so fulfilled and happy. Learning something new is always such a joy.$1",
  "Monika.Reaction5.1": "Wumbus? Never heard that word before. I wonder if the movie will be as interesting as its name.",
  "Monika.Reaction5.2": "Monika watches the tire-like green figures on the screen, her eyes crinkling, a small smile playing at her lips.",
  "Monika.Reaction5.3": "How fun! @~ A sci-fi movie full of modern humor. I love it~$1#$b#I really enjoyed our movie date today. Thanks for spending it with me~$10",
  "Monika.Reaction6.1": "Well, so it's a horror movie? I hope it's got something that'll actually impress me.$7",
  "Monika.Reaction6.2": "Monika sits there unmoved. The horror on screen looks to her like a child making silly faces.",
  "Monika.Reaction6.3": "@, remember when we talked about horror movies in the Literature Club?$7#$b#I do love horror novels myself, but horror movies are another story.$5#$b#Horror movies have no craft. They just use scary sounds, images, and jump scares to trigger that primal fear instinct. Pretty pointless.$11#$b#But don't worry, @, I'm not mad at you. Thank you for taking the time to watch with me. That alone is enough for me.$4",
  "Monika.Reaction7.1": "A black-and-white poster. Looks like a classic old film.$0#$b#If it can be remastered for modern theaters, I'm looking forward to the surprises it has in store~$1",
  "Monika.Reaction7.2": "I search with little hope, knowing legends don't exist...$4",
  "Monika.Reaction7.3": "You know, @, the young woman in the movie resonates with me deeply. She reminds me of my 'The Lady who Knows Everything,' and of my former self.$4#$b#I was once caught in the same conflict between reason and emotion, just as lost in the emptiness.$7#$b#But here's where we differ: at the film's end, she still doesn't know where that train of feeling is headed.$4#$b#I, on the other hand, found my ultimate answer long ago.$4#$b#Thank you for taking me to see this, @. What a wonderful surprise!$1",
