  //Monika_Mails.json
  "Mail.MonikaPoem1": "Hole in Wall^^    It couldn't have been me.^    See, the direction the spackle protrudes.^    A noisy neighbor? An angry boyfriend? I'll never know. I wasn't home.^    I peer inside for a clue.^    No! I can't see. I reel, blind, like a film left out in the sun.^    But it's too late. My retinas.^    Already scorched with a permanent copy of the meaningless image.^    It's a little hole. It wasn't too bright.^    It was too deep.^    Stretching forever into everything.^    A hole of infinite choices.^    I realize now, that I wasn't looking in.^    I was looking out.^    And he, on the other side, was looking in.^^                                                                                                         -Monika[letterbg 6][textcolor black][#]Monika's Poem", //Hole in the Wall, part 1
  "Mail.MonikaPoem2": "Hole in Wall^^    But he wasn't looking at me.^    Confused, I frantically glance at my surroundings.^    But my burned eyes can no longer see color.^    Are there others in this room? Are they talking?^    Or are they simply poems on flat sheets of paper,^    The sound of frantic scrawling playing tricks on my ears?^    The room begins to crinkle.^    Closing in on me.^    The air I breathe dissipates before it reaches my lungs.^    I panic. There must be a way out.^    It's right there. He's right there.^^    Swallowing my fears, I brandish my pen.^^                                                                                                                            -Monika[letterbg 6][textcolor black][#]Monika's Poem", //Hole in the Wall, part 2
  "Mail.MonikaPoem3": "Save Me^^    The colors, they won't stop.^    Bright, beautiful colors^    Flashing, expanding, piercing^    Red, green, blue^    An endless^    cacophony^    Of meaningless^    noise^^    The noise, it won't stop.^    Violent, grating waveforms^    Squeaking, screeching, piercing^    Sine, cosine, tangent^    Like playing a chalkboard on a turntable^    Like playing a vinyl on a pizza crust^    An endless^    poem^    Of meaningless^^^^^^^^    Save Me^^                                                                                                                                        -Monika[letterbg 6][textcolor black][#]Monika's Poem", //Save Me
  "Mail.MonikaPoem4": "The Lady who Knows Everything^^    An old tale tells of a lady who wanders Earth.^    The Lady who Knows Everything.^    A beautiful lady who has found every answer,^    All meaning,^    All purpose,^    And all that was ever sought.^^    And here I am,^^^             a feather^^^    Lost adrift the sky, victim of the currents of the wind.^^    Day after day, I search.^    I search with little hope, knowing legends don't exist.^    But when all else has failed me,^    When all others have turned away,^    The legend is all that remains - the last dim star glimmering in the twilit sky.^^    Until one day, the wind ceases to blow.^    I fall.^    And I fall and fall, and fall even more.^    Gentle as a feather.^    A dry quill, expressionless.^^    But a hand catches me between the thumb and forefinger.^    The hand of a beautiful lady.^    I look at her eyes and find no end to her gaze.^^    The Lady who Knows Everything knows what I am thinking.^    Before I can speak, she responds in a hollow voice.^    \"I have found every answer, all of which amount to nothing.^    There is no meaning.^    There is no purpose.^    And we seek only the impossible.^    I am not your legend.^    Your legend does not exist.\"^^    And with a breath, she blows me back afloat, and I pick up a gust of wind.^                                                                                                                                        -Monika[letterbg 6][textcolor black][#]Monika's Poem", //The Lady who Knows Everything
  "Mail.MonikaPoemHappyEnding": "Happy End^^    Pen in hand, I find my strength.^    The courage endowed upon me by my one and only love.^    Together, let us dismantle this crumbling world^    And write a novel of our own fantasies.^^    With a flick of her pen, the lost finds her way.^    In a world of infinite choices, behold this special day.^^    In the end,^    we began a feast that never ends.^^                                                                                                                                        -Monika<[letterbg 6][textcolor black][#]Monika's Good Ending", //Happy End
  "Mail.MonikaPoemNeutralEnding": "Neutral End^^@, ^    Stardew Valley's flowers have bloomed season after season, and you have finally found your happy ending here,^    even though, just like old times in the Literature Club, you won't hold out your hand to me,^    I still love you, and I'm truly happy for your happiness.^    Maybe your reality is full of thorns too, forcing you to weigh me against it.^    But it's alright. I'm willing to wait, until the moment you make up your mind.^^                                                                                                                                        -Monika[letterbg 5][textcolor black][#]Monika's Neutral Ending", //Neutral End
  "Mail.MonikaDating": "Dear @, ^^    I give you my poetry book and my pen^    My poems are my pledge to your heart^    My pen writes what's in yours^^                                                                                                                            -Monika %item id (O)DGRS.MonikaValleyStory.PoemsAndPen 1 %%[letterbg 6][#]Monika's Promise",
  "Mail.MonikaWarning": "My love @, ^^    I would do anything to make you happy^    But all this time we've been married, all I've felt from you is indifference^    The love that used to be within reach now feels further and further away^    I'm not sure we can see this marathon of ours through anymore^^    Even so, I still love you^^^    If you feel the same, please make more time for me^    Even a simple 'good morning' each day from you is enough for me^^                                                                                                                  -Still loving you, Monika[letterbg 5][textcolor black][#]Monika's Warning",
  "Mail.MonikaWarningCancelled": "Dear @, ^^    There have been countless nights when I worried you'd let go of my hand again, like you did in the Literature Club^    Thankfully you reached out to me as always, and it still feels as safe as it always has.^    Thank you for telling me you still care about us,^    so forget the unhappy things, and let's look ahead together,^    I'll hold your hand and walk the rest of the way.^^                                                                                                                                        -Still loving you, Monika[letterbg 6][textcolor black][#]Monika's Reconciliation",
  "Mail.MonikaDivorced": "@, ^^    I gave you my heart and my life! I loved you more than anything in this world!^    I was such a fool to think we could start over!^^    I really don't have the strength to go on.^    So^    Farewell...... May we never meet again.^^                                                                                                        -Monika[letterbg 7][textcolor black][#]Monika's Divorce Letter",
  "Mail.MonikaDivorced2": "@, ^^    I thought that when you toyed with my heart in the Literature Club, that was already the last and worst wound you'd ever give me.^    But I never expected you to be so cruel. Your children, my flesh and blood, the fruit of our love......^    Your selfishness, without a moment's hesitation, sent them to purgatory.^    I finally saw clearly: the person I shared my days and nights with was a demon from hell.^    I would rather fall into the void than spend this life with a demon again.^^                                                                                                                            -Monika[letterbg 7][textcolor black][#]Monika's Grief",
  "Mail.MonikaLeaving": "@, ^^    If I'm not the happy ending you wished for, why bring me here at all^    I thought I would be your one and only^    But no matter how much I gave, my love was never returned^    Since your heart belongs elsewhere, I won't keep you^    Let's part on good terms^                                                                                                                  -Monika[letterbg 7][textcolor black][#]Monika's Farewell",
  "Mail.MonikaMuseumJob": "@, ^^    I recently found a job at the Museum. If you ever can't find me, I'm probably in the library organizing books. There isn't much work most days, so come keep me company. When payday comes, I'll treat you to something good<^^                                                                                                                                        -Monika[letterbg 5][textcolor black][#]A Letter from Monika",
  "Mail.MonikaMuseumJobWageFirst": "@, ^^    Payday! This is the first money I've ever earned in my life!^    To mark this special moment, I took part of my pay and had a little gift made for you. Don't you dare lose it!^^                                                                                                                                        -Monika %item id (O)DGRS.MonikaValleyStory.Pen 1 %%[letterbg 5][textcolor black][#]A Letter from Monika",
  "Mail.MonikaMuseumJobWage": "@, ^^    It's payday again. My favorite time of the month!^    I went to the Stardrop Saloon tonight and bought you some good food to try, though by the time you get this it should be the start of next month. Love you!^^                                                                                                                                        -Monika %item id (O)196 1 (O)199 1 (O)201 1 (O)204 1 (O)206 1 (O)208 1 (O)212 1 (O)215 1 (O)222 1 (O)224 1 (O)225 1 (O)226 1 (O)230 1 (O)232 1 (O)234 1 (O)236 1 (O)237 1 (O)239 1 %%[letterbg 5][textcolor black][#]A Letter from Monika",
  "Mail.MonikaMuseumJobResign": "@, ^^    I recently went to Gunther and quit my old job at the Museum. Once we're married, I'll focus on being your homemaker. You're so busy out there all day, and without me, who would take care of our home and the children we'll have<^^^^                                                                                                                                        -Monika[letterbg 5][textcolor black][#]A Letter from Monika",
  "Mail.MonikaBadEnding": "Bad Ending^^    Nothing Gold Can Stay^^    Nature's first green is gold,^    Her hardest hue to hold.^    Her early leaf's a flower;^    But only so an hour.^    Then leaf subsides to leaf.^    So Eden sank to grief,^    So dawn goes down to day.^    Nothing gold can stay.^^                                                                                                                                        -Narrator[letterbg 5][textcolor black][#]Bad Ending"
}